Topi, I _can_ do elementary predicate calculus and basic 
stochastics[1].  The point is that Prob(spe <= otmp->spe) 
is very small if x>0; in fact it is orders of magnitude 
smaller than Prob(spe <= rnd(5)) for armours and weapons.  
And consequently, as I wrote, the test (spe > otmp->spe) 
plays almost no role and could just as well be left out, 
since it changes the results only by a relative factor 
of about 10^{-3}.  (If x <5, that is; in the other 
cases, (spe > otmp->spe) has such a small success probability 
that you would on the average have to wish ~7940 times to get 
a +6 granted once, which is more or less the same as a 
zero chance.  It simply does not affect the game measurably.)  
Calculate it for yourself if you don't believe me.  

